        "title": "Qiang Zhu",
        "excerpt":"Qiang Zhu (ORCiD: 0000-0002-9892-0344)is an Associate Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineerng and Energy Scienceat the University of North Carolina at Charlotte (UNCC). Prior to joining UNCC, he was an Associate Professor in the Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of Nevada, Las Vegas (UNLV) between 2016 and 2023. Qiang holds a Ph.D. in Mineral Physics from the State University of New York at Stony Brook, as well as a B.S. in Materials Science and Engineering from Beijing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics in China. He is also the recipients of 2021 Early Career Awards from both the National Science Foundation (NSF) and the U.S. Department of Energy (DOE).   Education     2009-2013 - Ph.D. in Mineral Physics, Stony Brook University.   2003-2007 - B.S. in Materials Sciences Engineering, Beihang University   Ph.D. Dissertation  Crystal structure prediction and its application in Earth and Materials Sciences (Stony Brook University, 2013)  ","categories": [],
